Case
-- CASE is a conditional expression in SQL that works like an if-else or switch statement.
-- It returns different values based on different conditions — all within a single query.

WHY DO WE USE CASE?
-- To create custom columns on-the-fly
-- To categorize data based on certain logic
-- To replace values conditionally
-- To handle nulls or missing values gracefully
-- To simplify complex logic inside SELECT queries

syntax :
select column_name,
case when condition1 then result1
     when condition2 then result2
     when condition3 then result3
     else default_result
end as new_column_name from table_name;

eg1 :
Add a custom column in which you will have price_tag.
If the price is above 1000, you will say it is expensive.
If the price is between 500 and 1000, you will say it is moderate.
If the price is below 500, it is cheap.
show name and price as well
solution :
select name, price,
case when (price > 1000) then 'Expensive'
	 when (price between 500 and 1000) then 'Moderate'
	 else'Cheap'
end as "price_tag" from products;
-- This is just a virtual data not the real data. I mean this will not alter the table.
-- to add it permanently we have to go through few steps :
# 1st step : Create a new column
alter table products add column price_tag text;
-- now all the values here are null
# 2nd step : Update the column using case
update products set price_tag =
case
  when (price > 1000) then 'Expensive'
  when (price between 500 and 1000) then 'Moderate'
	else 'Cheap'
end;

eg2 :
Inside the is_available column, you have boolean values (true and false).
Show a new column using CASE with values 'In Stock' and 'Out of Stock' with name and price.
solution:
select name,price, is_available,
case
  when is_available = 'true' then 'In Stock'
  else 'Out of Stock'
end as "Availability" from products;

eg 3: HIGHLIGHT STOCK STATUS
Show product name, stock quantity, and label:
"High Stock" if quantity > 100
"Medium Stock" if between 30 and 100
"Low Stock" otherwise
solution :
select name, stock_quantity ,
case
  when stock_quantity > 100 then 'High Stock'
  when stock_quantity between 30 and 100 then 'Medium Stock'
  else 'Low Stock'
end as "stock_status" from products;
